shadowfetch-menus (2.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release, for Shadowfetch Linux 2.1.2 "Fire Edition".
  * Seven-category launcher as an XDG merge-dir drop-in
    (/etc/xdg/menus/applications-merged/shadowfetch-launcher.menu):
    Create, Develop, Communicate, Play, Protect, System, AI and Agents.
    The stock top-level menus are deleted in the merge; the Lost & Found
    (OnlyUnallocated) catch-all is preserved, and the QEMU gate for the
    release is that it stays empty over the full ISO app set.
  * The merge-dir route is deliberate: startplasma sets XDG_MENU_PREFIX
    unconditionally and kservice hardcodes applications-merged/, so an
    own-prefix menu file can never be reached. kmenuedit user edits
    always win over this drop-in (stock DefaultMergeDirs merges before
    the kmenuedit MergeFile), and plasma-workspace's conffile is never
    touched.
  * Seven matching .directory files in /usr/share/desktop-directories.
  * The /usr/local/share/applications duplicate-cleanup overrides ride
    the ISO's live-build includes.chroot, not this package: Debian
    policy keeps /usr/local out of debs, and the admin namespace is what
    makes the overrides survive package upgrades.

 -- Shadowfetch Project <signing@shadowfetch.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:47:33 -0400
